# A-CureXpress environment variables, grouped by app.
#
# Each app reads its own apps/<app>/.env.local (Next.js loads env files from the app folder, not
# the repo root). Copy apps/<app>/.env.example to apps/<app>/.env.local and fill it in.
# Local values come from `pnpm supabase status`. Never commit real values.
# All three apps use ONE Supabase project per environment (local, staging, production).
#
# apps/web      (acurexpress.com, dev :3000)           see apps/web/.env.example
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (server only)
#   FLAG_MEDICINE_SALES, FLAG_ONLINE_PRESCRIBING, FLAG_AI_CONSULTANT, FLAG_NATIVE_APP_FEATURES,
#   FLAG_SHOP_NETWORK
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PARTNER_URL (footer partner band; dev default http://partners.localhost:3001; band hidden in production if missing)
#   Sign-in: AUTH_METHODS, NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY,
#   RATE_LIMIT_HMAC_SECRET (server only), CRON_SECRET (server only). See docs/AUTH.md.
#   The auth e2e suite writes its own git-ignored apps/web/.env.test.local (scripts/auth-e2e-env.sh).
#   later: PAYMENTS_*, SMS_*, NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPS_PUBLIC_KEY, MAPS_SERVER_KEY, VIDEO_*, AI_*
#
# apps/partner  (partners.acurexpress.com, dev :3001)  see apps/partner/.env.example
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, FLAG_* (same names as web)
#
# apps/admin    (admin.acurexpress.com, dev :3002)     see apps/admin/.env.example
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (server only, optional)
#
# Repo-level (no app): E2E_PORT overrides the Playwright port (web 3100, partner 3101, admin 3102).
# The auth e2e suite uses port 3200 and build folder .next-auth (NEXT_DIST_DIR).
#
# supabase/.env (git-ignored, see supabase/.env.example): SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
#   SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET, SUPABASE_AUTH_CAPTCHA_SECRET (local CLI only).
